.TH DISKCAPD 1 "August 2026" "diskcapd 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diskcapd \- monitor local filesystem capacity and availability
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diskcapd
.RI [ --version ]
.RI { discover , setup , status , check , test-notification }
.PP
.B diskcapd discover
.PP
.B diskcapd setup
.RI [ --config
.IR PATH ]
.PP
.B diskcapd status
.RI [ --config
.IR PATH ]
.PP
.B diskcapd check
.RI [ --config
.IR PATH ]
.RI [ --state
.IR PATH ]
.RI [ --quiet ]
.PP
.B diskcapd test-notification
.B --to
.I ADDRESS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diskcapd
monitors mounted writable local block-backed filesystems for capacity,
mount availability, and filesystem identity changes.
.PP
Configured filesystems are identified by mount point and filesystem UUID.
This allows diskcapd to detect a missing mount or an unexpected filesystem
mounted at a monitored location.
.PP
Network filesystems, pseudo filesystems, read-only mounts, swap, and other
non-local filesystem types are not eligible for monitoring.
.PP
Notifications are delivered through the system Postout profile named
.BR diskcapd .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B discover
List mounted writable local block-backed filesystems that are eligible for
monitoring.
.TP
.B setup
Configure the filesystems to monitor, the Postout notification profile,
and optional unattended monitoring.
When using the default system configuration, setup can enable and start
.BR diskcapd.timer
after configuration is complete.
The default configuration file is
.BR /etc/diskcapd/diskcapd.conf .
.TP
.B status
Show the current status of configured monitored filesystems without
performing the normal monitoring transaction.
.TP
.B check
Check configured filesystems, evaluate monitoring state, and process
notifications for alerts, reminders, and recoveries.
.TP
.B test-notification
Send a test notification through the configured system Postout profile.
The recipient must be supplied with
.BR --to .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show command help and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show the diskcapd version and exit.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Use an alternate configuration file.
The default is
.BR /etc/diskcapd/diskcapd.conf .
.TP
.BI --state " PATH"
Use an alternate monitoring state file for
.BR check .
The default is
.BR /var/lib/diskcapd/state.json .
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress steady-state output and show state transitions and errors only.
This mode is suitable for unattended systemd execution.
.TP
.BI --to " ADDRESS"
Send a test notification to the specified email address.
.SH MONITORING MODEL
For each configured filesystem, diskcapd checks that the expected mount is
present, is backed by an eligible local block device, has the expected
filesystem UUID, and remains within its configured capacity threshold.
.PP
A configured mount point is never silently replaced by information from a
parent filesystem when the expected mount disappears.
.PP
Monitoring state is persisted between checks so that diskcapd can distinguish
new violations, continuing violations, and recoveries.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
diskcapd sends three kinds of monitoring notifications:
.TP
.B ALERT
Sent when a filesystem enters a violation state or changes from one violation
condition to another.
.TP
.B REMINDER
Sent when a violation remains unresolved for 24 hours after the previous
successful alert or reminder.
.TP
.B RECOVERY
Sent when a previously violated filesystem returns to a healthy state.
.PP
Transitions detected during one check are aggregated into a single
notification.
.PP
Monitoring state is committed only after required notification delivery
succeeds. A notification failure therefore does not silently advance the
recorded notification state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/diskcapd/diskcapd.conf
System monitoring configuration.
.TP
.B /var/lib/diskcapd/state.json
Persistent monitoring state.
.TP
.B /etc/postout/profiles.json
System Postout profile configuration used for notification delivery.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully. For
.BR check ,
no filesystem violation was present.
.TP
.B 1
The check completed and one or more filesystem violations were present.
.TP
.B 2
A configuration or operational error occurred.
.TP
.B 3
Notification delivery failed.
.SH SYSTEMD
The Debian package installs:
.TP
.B diskcapd.service
A oneshot service that runs
.BR "diskcapd check --quiet" .
.TP
.B diskcapd.timer
A systemd timer for periodic monitoring.
.PP
The timer is not started automatically on a fresh installation.
After setup and validation, enable monitoring with:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl enable --now diskcapd.timer
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
List eligible filesystems:
.PP
.nf
diskcapd discover
.fi
.PP
Configure diskcapd:
.PP
.nf
sudo diskcapd setup
.fi
.PP
Inspect monitoring status:
.PP
.nf
sudo diskcapd status
.fi
.PP
Run a scheduler-style check:
.PP
.nf
sudo diskcapd check --quiet
.fi
.PP
Test notification delivery:
.PP
.nf
sudo diskcapd test-notification --to admin@example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR postout (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR findmnt (8)
